  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>According to the town hall, La Londe-les-Maures has three concession beaches (Miramar, Tamaris, Argentière), plus Pellegrin and Pansard, nearly 3 km of fine sand in all. None is named "Bormettes beach": that name refers to a neighbourhood of the town around the old factory and its theatre, not to a beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Several unofficial guides (France 3 Régions 2023, a 2026 dog-beach guide) cite a dog area between Tamaris beach and Argentière beach, marked by a sign. We found no mention of dogs on the "Les plages" pages of the town hall or the tourist office, and the beach policing order (2024) is only available as an unreadable scan: the exact rule (leash, hours, season) is therefore not confirmed. A specialised site dated June 2026 says dogs are no longer accepted on Argentière itself, without confirmation from the town hall. Call the town hall (04 94 01 55 00) before coming.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: stay outside the supervised swimming areas and keep your dog on a leash, as a precaution.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cani Plouf in Le Pradet is about twenty minutes away by car if this area isn't accessible.</p>
